        <headline>Flood Warning issued September 25 at 4:06AM EDT until September 25 at 4:15AM EDT by NWS Charleston WV</headline>
        <description>The Flood Warning will expire at 415 AM EDT early this morning for a
portion of central West Virginia, including the following county,
Calhoun.

Flood waters are receding, so the Flood Warning is being allowed to
expire. However, motorists should continue to exercise extreme
caution and be prepared for water or debris remaining on roadways.
Please continue to heed remaining road closures.
</description>
